involved in the illness process, they can stimu-late the defence
system to attack and in this way fight the illness. This might explain
why urine therapy has proven so helpful in treating allergies. The
practise of drinking and massaging with urine allows antibodies
greater ac-cess to the body, which stimulates the immune system.
Applying urine to a fresh cut or scrape prevents infection and keeps
flies away (important in coun-tries with a warm climate). Urine
compresses from fresh or old urine help to combat infections and often
cause them to disappear. Although urine does not entirely prevent the
